{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/mCVc7zAazC3OhAdz6DptVZrmCnH.jpg","genre_ids":[35],"id":67,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"What's Happening Now!!","overview":"Roger 'Raj' Thomas has graduated from the University of Southern California, and become a fledgling writer. He and his wife Nadine, a social worker, move in to his old home in Watts (given to him by his mother, Mabel, now remarried and living in Phoenix, Arizona). His sister Dee is away at college. Childhood friend Dwayne Nelson has become a computer programmer, while Freddie 'Rerun' Stubbs is a used-car salesman. The old soda shop hangout, Rob's Place, has gone out of business and left abandoned. Reminded of his youth, and seeing an opportunity, Raj and Shirley Wilson, who used to wait tables there, decide to buy the business together, renaming it Rob's.","popularity":8.8351,"poster_path":"/3jAdacJlx81TNdN26eucSaGBcCr.jpg","first_air_date":"1985-09-07","softcore":false,"name":"What's Happening Now!!","vote_average":6.6,"vote_count":12},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/sS0WV6clFjHMQMdGMpg6X4qsKBA.jpg","genre_ids":[35],"id":31,"origin_country":["GB"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"French Fields","overview":"French Fields is a British situation comedy. It ran for 19 episodes from 5 September 1989 to 8 October 1991. It was written by John T. Chapman and Ian Davidson and was produced by Thames Television for ITV.\n\nThe series starred Anton Rodgers and Julia McKenzie as husband and wife William and Hester Fields and followed the series Fresh Fields, which ran from 7 March 1984 to 23 October 1986. At the end of the last series of Fresh Fields, William accepted a position with a French company. French Fields follows Hester and William after they make the move to Calais.\n\nOther regular cast included their French real estate agent Chantal, who was also the Fields' neighbour to the left. On the right, were the horrible and snobbish English couple the Trendles. Hester and William also coped with Madame Remoleux, an unintelligible and ancient French woman who lived in and cared for the estate — called Les Hirondelles — where they all lived. Also, popping in on a regular basis, were local farmer and mayor Monsieur Dax and his daughter Marie-Christine, to whom Hester did her best to teach English. Nicholas Courtney also appeared frequently as the Marquis.","popularity":5.1042,"poster_path":"/lyHrZcumijZ37J4f2ioMEtoZswb.jpg","first_air_date":"1989-09-05","softcore":false,"name":"French Fields","vote_average":6.9,"vote_count":7},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/6zzyWTu3p2Diztotbnb0kf128uo.jpg","genre_ids":[35,10751,18],"id":47,"origin_country":["MX"],"original_language":"es","original_name":"El Chavo del Ocho","overview":"The mishaps of Chavo, an 8-year-old Mestizo-Latino American orphan boy who lives in a village. Together with Quico, Chilindrina, Ñoño and La Popis, Chavo experiences a series of humorous entanglements.","popularity":36.7836,"poster_path":"/1TdBpVOASafzfWlnecwW17UL6a5.jpg","first_air_date":"1973-02-26","softcore":false,"name":"El Chavo del Ocho","vote_average":8.1,"vote_count":2088},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/cBJDOCMFAV4Ls8nZLRRj424RgID.jpg","genre_ids":[10759,18,10765,10762],"id":203,"origin_country":["GB"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"The Sarah Jane Adventures","overview":"Sarah Jane Smith is a truly remarkable woman who inhabits a world of mystery, danger and wonder; a world where aliens are commonplace and the Earth is under constant threat. A world that Maria Jackson, a seemingly ordinary girl, can only dream of – until she moves in next door. Nothing will ever be ordinary again.","popularity":18.8911,"poster_path":"/hq0S1VtUabnORdp3l3m11OA67BP.jpg","first_air_date":"2007-09-24","softcore":false,"name":"The Sarah Jane Adventures","vote_average":7.1,"vote_count":117},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/s1Kr1RntP2b8MdUKTYJxNmcVEBP.jpg","genre_ids":[10759,16,35,10762],"id":160,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles","overview":"Four turtles fall into the sewers and are befriended by Hamato Yoshi a Japanese man sent to New York who was forced to live in the sewers. One day he sees a strange green glow which transforms the four turtles into human-like creatures. Hamato (now Master Splinter) changes into a giant rat from the green glow and teaches the turtles the skills of the ninja as they team up with news reporter April O'Neil to battle against Yoshi's arch enemy Shredder and Krang, an alien warlord from Dimension X.","popularity":50.7781,"poster_path":"/AaihPizftZo5YCqzEgHMwkceaEo.jpg","first_air_date":"1987-12-14","softcore":false,"name":"Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles","vote_average":7.8,"vote_count":871},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/ywK4VrR7vL56mDGXDLMtFypwqA8.jpg","genre_ids":[10765,18],"id":253,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Star Trek","overview":"Space. The Final Frontier. The U.S.S. Enterprise embarks on a five year mission to explore the galaxy. The Enterprise is under the command of Captain James T. Kirk with First Officer Mr. Spock, from the planet Vulcan. With a determined crew, the Enterprise encounters Klingons, Romulans, time paradoxes, tribbles and genetic supermen led by Khan Noonian Singh. Their mission is to explore strange new worlds, to seek new life and new civilizations, and to boldly go where no man has gone before.","popularity":82.0914,"poster_path":"/9byecLwsbbkAqGdxcKuuTI5kEzZ.jpg","first_air_date":"1966-09-08","softcore":false,"name":"Star Trek","vote_average":8,"vote_count":1575},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/qeJUqoZZj0JUPcOhU0tseLoNFtX.jpg","genre_ids":[35,10751],"id":248,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"So Little Time","overview":"So Little Time is an American sitcom starring Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen that aired on Fox Family. The first half of the series aired from June 2, 2001, to August 15, 2001. The series then went on a four-month hiatus owing to network management changes. By December 2001, Fox Family had become ABC Family, and the remaining episodes aired until May 4, 2002.","popularity":7.5918,"poster_path":"/iNkK6WIixZlJNlMu912ngUOYTmF.jpg","first_air_date":"2001-06-02","softcore":false,"name":"So Little Time","vote_average":7.5,"vote_count":31},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/2zdd8K73kRGXYIe1BT1ne6eIh4N.jpg","genre_ids":[16,10762,10751],"id":345,"origin_country":["JP","US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"My Little Pony","overview":"Ponyland is the home of all your favorite classic Little Ponies. Together, they live a life of games, songs and harmony with allies like the Bushwoolies and Furbobs. But, occasionally, there are problems in Ponyland and the Little Ponies of Paradise Estate must face evil witches, goblins, Stone Backs, Grundles and more!","popularity":15.4161,"poster_path":"/tkVztC8YKR8JSIHgwRWD5boViBJ.jpg","first_air_date":"1986-09-15","softcore":false,"name":"My Little Pony","vote_average":6.6,"vote_count":22},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/5LU77x2BK2IFn0hhyA8GbqjzMt4.jpg","genre_ids":[16,35,10759,10751,10765,10762],"id":346,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"American Dragon: Jake Long","overview":"American Dragon is a coming of age comedy-action series about Jake Long, a 13-year-old Asian-American boy who strives to find balance in his life as a skateboard-grinding, New York 'tween while learning to master his mystical powers (in his secret identity) as the American Dragon, the protector and guardian of all magical creatures secretly living amidst the human world.","popularity":21.7438,"poster_path":"/x2Wd9ZuCYxbx8G2hwOhW3fuKEku.jpg","first_air_date":"2005-01-21","softcore":false,"name":"American Dragon: Jake Long","vote_average":7.8,"vote_count":533},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/uwDpjQDl8agkdvsTnD08mmIFUIk.jpg","genre_ids":[35],"id":420,"origin_country":["GB"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Whatever Happened to the Likely Lads?","overview":"Whatever Happened to the Likely Lads? is a British sitcom which was broadcast between 9 January 1973 and 9 April 1974 on BBC1. It was the colour sequel to the mid-1960s hit The Likely Lads. It was created and written, as was its predecessor, by Dick Clement and Ian La Frenais. There were 26 television episodes over two series; and a subsequent 45-minute Christmas special was aired on 24 December 1974.\n\nThe cast were reunited in 1975 for a BBC radio adaptation of series 1, transmitted on Radio 4 from July to October that year. In 1976, a feature film spin-off was made. Around the time of its release, however, Rodney Bewes and James Bolam fell out over a misunderstanding involving the press and have not spoken since. This long-suspected situation was finally confirmed by Bewes while promoting his autobiography in 2005. Unlike Bewes, Bolam is consistently reluctant to talk about the show, and has vetoed any attempt to revive his character.","popularity":6.8215,"poster_path":"/n9F822PC6D3rpbN89ztZPBDTeWf.jpg","first_air_date":"1973-01-09","softcore":false,"name":"Whatever Happened to the Likely Lads?","vote_average":7.7,"vote_count":22},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/A8We2BSM6hJ1VWzncssnU2fFsft.jpg","genre_ids":[16,10759,10765],"id":513,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Batman Beyond","overview":"As new villains overrun Gotham City of the future, the aging Bruce Wayne hangs up the cape of the once invincible Batman. But when troubled teenager Terry McGinnis stumbles upon the Dark Knight's secret, a new alliance is forged. And a triumphant new Batman is born.","popularity":37.3863,"poster_path":"/d01V9s1hjYYJwAeocLNmrhY0ToU.jpg","first_air_date":"1999-01-10","softcore":false,"name":"Batman Beyond","vote_average":8.167,"vote_count":640},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/6neiLkVRYIVbbRTLhlSLtt8o5di.jpg","genre_ids":[16,35,18,10751],"id":537,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language